From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Germino <jasongermino@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] video: sunxi: AW_DISP2 must not default to y

AW_DISP2 is the legacy sunxi-disp2 framebuffer display driver.  It does not
build on 6.6 and would conflict with the DRM display driver (sunxi-drm) that
this board uses.  Its Kconfig entry says "depends on AW_PWM" and "default y",
so it was off only because the PWM driver (AW_PWM) was off.  Turning AW_PWM on
(needed for the fan header) would silently turn the legacy driver on as well.

Make it opt-in.  The board config also lists it explicitly as not set, and
scripts/check-image.sh fails a build if it is ever enabled.

Signed-off-by: Jason Germino <jasongermino@gmail.com>
---
 bsp/drivers/video/sunxi/Kconfig | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/bsp/drivers/video/sunxi/Kconfig b/bsp/drivers/video/sunxi/Kconfig
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/bsp/drivers/video/sunxi/Kconfig
+++ b/bsp/drivers/video/sunxi/Kconfig
@@ -18,7 +18,7 @@ config AW_DISP2
 	tristate "DISP Driver Support(sunxi-disp2)"
 #	depends on (ARCH_SUNXI)
 	depends on AW_PWM
-	default y
+	default n
 	select DMA_SHARED_BUFFER
 	help
 	  Display driver for sunxi based boards.
